---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import InfoPage from "@components/InfoPage.astro";
import { IS_LIVE } from "@lib/config";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Voting Rules | NepalRanks"
  description="The NepalRanks voting rules: one vote per ranking, three votes per site, per rolling 24 hours, with vote switching and anti-manipulation policy."
>
  <InfoPage eyebrow="Rules">
    <h1>Voting rules</h1>
    <p>
      Voting is the product. These rules exist so that a ranking reflects many
      small human opinions rather than a few loud automated ones.
    </p>

    <h2>The rolling 24-hour allowance</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Each account gets <strong>3 votes per rolling 24-hour window across the whole site</strong> (not a calendar day: each vote's window closes 24 hours after that vote).</li>
      <li><strong>One vote per ranking</strong>: your 3 votes must go to 3 different rankings. An upvote or a downvote, never both on the same item.</li>
      <li>Switching from up to down (or the reverse) within the window replaces the previous vote; it does not consume a second slot.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How a vote changes a ranking</h2>
    <p>
      Net score = upvotes minus downvotes. Entries on a ranking page are sorted by net
      score at all times. There is no minimum threshold, no decay weighting and no
      administrator override; the arithmetic is the ranking.
    </p>

    <h2>Fair play</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>One person, one account. Coordinated vote-farming, bots and bought votes are removed and the operator is sanctioned.</li>
      <li>Entries are ranked on the merit of the service or place, not on advertising spend, advertising is not sold on rankings at all.</li>
      <li>Businesses may be listed, never privileged. A bank's owner votes exactly like a student.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Comment voting</h2>
    <p>
      Comments carry their own up/down score with a lighter allowance; three top
      comments per entry are surfaced on ranking pages. Comment voting never moves
      an entry's ranking position.
    </p>

    <h2>Status of these rules</h2>
    <p>
      {IS_LIVE
        ? "Voting and commenting require a one-click Google sign-in, your limits follow your account, not your browser. Votes and comments count instantly, and this page re-sorts as scores change."
        : "This deployment has no live service attached, the vote buttons demonstrate the intended interaction only and nothing is recorded."}
    </p>
  </InfoPage>
</BaseLayout>
